The Koch Internship Program (KIP) is a paid experiential learning program run by Stand Together Fellowships that offers professional development, leadership training, and meaningful work experience at non-profits tackling some of our nation's most pressing policy challenges all over the United States. Early-career professionals including undergraduate/graduate/law students and recent graduates are encouraged to apply. Eligible candidates will be geographically located in and authorized to work in the United States through the duration of the program. Successful candidates will interview with both our non-profit partner organizations and Stand Together Fellowships staff, so we strongly encourage you to begin the admissions process early!

About Taxpayers Protection Alliance Foundation 
The Taxpayers Protection Alliance Foundation (TPAF) is a non-profit, non-partisan organization dedicated to educating the public about the effects of excessive taxation and spending by all levels of government through research, investigative reporting, and analysis. TPAF also educates the public about government transparency and openness in the United States and around the world.
About the role
The Taxpayers Protection Alliance Foundation (TPAF) is seeking a highly motivated part-time intern to join our communications team. Candidates should have an interest in economic and regulatory policy areas now being debated in Congress and within the executive branch as well as a strong commitment to free-market economics and limited government.
An ideal candidate will have strong writing skills. Previous experience in digital media is preferred but not required.
This role will be part-time, in person, in Washington, D.C.
Primary Responsibilities:
Drafting creative copy for the organization’s X, Facebook, Instagram, and YouTube accounts, including rapid response content for breaking news;
Filming, editing, and producing short-form video content for social media;
Advising team on up-and-coming social media trends and developing creative ways to incorporate them into TPAF content to maximize reach and engagement;
Creating graphics and other visual content for TPAF’s social media platforms, campaigns, events, and other materials;
Attending various events in Washington, D.C. to promote the TPAF brand, capture content, and assist with live-tweeting;
Assisting the VP of Communications with press releases and media advisories as needed;
Updating press contacts for the organization, ensuring state and national broadcast and print pitching lists are accurate and complete

